---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Service Terms"
  description="Terms governing paid Meyppi campaign audits: scope, client obligations, confidentiality, ownership, liability limits, payment and governing law."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h1>Service Terms</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: 7 October 2026</p>

      <p>
        These terms govern paid campaign delivery audits supplied by
        Meyppi. They are referenced in every quote and engagement letter,
        which together form the agreement for each engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>Scope of an audit</h2>
      <p>
        An audit verifies whether contracted, pre-produced audio creatives
        appeared in independently observable published media: which
        placements ran, which version, at what position, and for how much
        of the contracted runtime. Scope, sources and any exclusions are
        confirmed in writing before work starts. Dynamic ad insertion,
        host-read verification, video sources and legal testimony are
        outside current scope.
      </p>

      <h2>Client obligations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Supply master creative files for every contracted version, the insertion order or placement plan, and campaign dates.</li>
        <li>Confirm the right to provide the creatives and any recordings supplied.</li>
        <li>Make media access available where the audit depends on it, and identify a contact for contract questions.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        Each party keeps the other's non-public material confidential and
        uses it only for the engagement. Client campaign material is not
        published or shared; findings belong to the commissioning party.
        A mutual NDA is available on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The client owns its creatives, media and the delivered report and
        evidence exports. Meyppi retains its methodology, engine and
        aggregate, non-identifying calibration knowledge. Published use of
        report excerpts is fine; please do not alter findings when quoting
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty of legal admissibility</h2>
      <p>
        Reports are algorithmic findings with documented methodology,
        evidence and confidence values. They are supplied as evidence for
        commercial reconciliation and reporting, without warranty of
        admissibility in any legal proceeding.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        A fixed quote per campaign is agreed in writing before work
        starts. Invoicing terms, including any advance and the invoice due
        period, are stated in the quote. Prices are exclusive of
        applicable taxes unless stated otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        Each party's aggregate liability under an engagement is capped at
        the fees paid for that engagement. Neither party is liable for
        indirect or consequential losses.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        Either party may terminate an engagement in writing; work
        completed to that date is invoiced pro rata and delivered
        material is handled per the retention terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        Governed by the laws of India, with exclusive jurisdiction in the
        courts of the city of Meyppi's registered office.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
